# Criteria declarations are tracked by git; logs and build artifacts are not.
#
# Logs are append-only: every observe appends an entry. That is the design, and it is exactly
# the shape that should not be committed. `sync` can rebuild logs from declarations, but it
# captures the current baseline, not the original run — historical replay from logs is not possible.
#
# Artifacts are locally built and carry platform-specific binary hashes, so they are not portable.
*
!.gitignore
!anchors.toml
!probes.toml
